# What must never reach the image, and why.
#
# .env is the deployment IDENTITY (FLEET_HOST/ALLOWED_HOSTS/SHARE_HOSTS/SHARE_URL and the
# owner's FLEET_CMD) — it is gitignored precisely because this repo is public, and an image
# is a more copyable artifact than a checkout. Same for the runtime state and ledgers: they
# carry the owner token, every lane self-token and every share secret (fleet.json), plus the
# audit trails. A container is supposed to START one of these, never to INHERIT one.
.env
fleet.json
fleet.json.*
fleet.pid
audit.jsonl*
steward-journal.jsonl*
lane-outcomes.jsonl*
dispositions.jsonl*
post-land-audits.jsonl*
post-land-audit-queue.json*
*.log

# CLAUDE.md/OWNER.md are gitignored owner documents, not app code.
CLAUDE.md
OWNER.md

# streams/ is the recorded pane output of the owner's real sessions — 43 MB of transcript-
# adjacent bytes with no business in an image.
streams/

# rebuilt inside the image (bun install / bun run build), so shipping the host's copies would
# ship darwin-arm64 artifacts into a linux-arm64 container.
node_modules/
public/app.js
public/share.js

# scratch and local tooling
e2e-trail/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/settings.local.json
